msgid "Store a *weak* reference to the owning dataset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/data_model.py:250
msgid ""
"This is a child-to-parent back reference, so it must not keep the dataset "
"alive.  A strong reference here leaks the whole dataset: when the Python "
"wrapper for this field data is released while the C++ object is still alive "
"(the common case -- ``ds.cell_data`` returns a temporary), ``vtkPythonUtil::"
"RemoveObjectFromMap`` stashes ``__dict__`` in the ghost map, which then pins "
"everything it references until the C++ object dies.  Since the dataset owns "
"this field data, that never happens, and the cycle is invisible to Python's "
"garbage collector. ``VTKDataArrayMixin._set_dataset`` uses the same weak "
"reference."
msgstr ""

